    "updated_at": "2020-06-11T17:53:13Z",
    "body": "Thank you for thorough explanation. I have no issues with authors assuming an accepted convention such as Oxford commas. To that end, I think this issue can be closed, for my part at least. I will have to learn Oxford commas thoroughly and keep these in mind reading WHATWG documents in depth :)\r\n\r\nPerhaps linking a \"how to interpret the specification(s)\"-kind of a document could be a thing to consider? It's hard for me to judge merits of such a thing -- the sentence in question may only be hard enough to interpret for a minority of people, like me. Or you could improve sentences in place, that sounds good too, although I'd imagine it'd be more effort. ",
