    "created_at": "2020-06-11T18:11:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-06-11T18:11:48Z",
    "body": "In general I don't think Oxford commas fully solve the problems of making boolean logic clear to the reader. Even when programming, if I mix together `&&` and `||` in a single expression I always put parenthesis around clauses appropriately. I think we should do the same here (with bulleted lists being a good prose counterpart).",
